Z||000000||Haze_Performance||07-31-2001||05:48 PM||||I have a challenge for you.<P>A while back I posted a body mod for the 84/86 coupe front nose. Cut out the black bumper pads (where they start to recess around the edges) & set the area back a few inches. Finish it off with a mesh grill. The can remain black (along with the grill) A new style turn signal can be installed the the same location just back on the mesh. Do ya follow me here? Its kinda hard to put into words.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">  <BR></A><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000001||AusFiero||07-31-2001||07:41 PM||||I think I know what you mean Haze. Only problem I have is I don't have access to any cars like that to play with. If sales go well on Stage-2 body kit, the next project is the 89 Hybrid. I have to make enough money off Stage 2 first to cover my costs, live, and to also buy a Fiero coupe to keep in the garage for development purposes. A cheap Fiero coupe still costs $5000 in this country. Well unless someone on the West Coast can sell me one real cheap and deliver it to LA. I only need a good body. I can then cut that cost down a little. Not much but a little. <P>Monkeyman has kindly donated one but costs associated to get it from Illinois to California kills any chance of using that one. Thanks anyway Monkeyman, your a good mate.<P>Then after that who knows. As time goes on and if sales go well I do eventually intend to keep a variety of different panels to enable me to develop items for all Fiero body styles.<P>This has pretty much turned into a full time business for me now. So if people keep buying items I will keep making different things.<P> By the way I am also an agent for MOMO now so anybody wants MOMO, give me a yell. I can beat the USA prices. <P>Have also kicked up a deal to supply a very nice looking Fiero Brake kit. 13" cross drilled gold zinc plated vented discs, 4 spot calipers etc etc for under $3000, as always including delivery and insurance. It is the Ryan Motorsport kit. My price is the same as theirs as I work on a comission deal with them, but I include the shipping and will be inclined to throw in the odd freebie here and there.<P>Anyway I am going out to the garage now to start cutting my templates up for Stage 2 Side Scoops.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
